WEBVTT

00:01.460 --> 00:04.570
Ikusen no namida o koe

00:04.570 --> 00:08.200
Omoi wa kouya o yuku

00:08.200 --> 00:16.130
Itsuka kizu wa ieru kara saa trust myself

00:21.280 --> 00:27.790
Yaketsuku hizashi no moto kimi wa nani omou?

00:27.790 --> 00:33.730
Urei no hitomi wa ima nani o utsusu?

00:33.730 --> 00:42.670
Mayowazu ni irareru no nara
step by step tayasui darou

00:42.670 --> 00:47.440
Kaze no you ni

00:47.440 --> 00:50.510
Ikusen no namida o koe

00:50.510 --> 00:54.120
Akatsuki no kouya o yuku

00:54.120 --> 01:00.560
Itsuka kizu wa ieru kara saa trust myself

01:00.560 --> 01:07.360
Don't be afraid kawaru koto wa
osoreru koto ja nai

01:07.360 --> 01:13.470
Kimi ga kimi de aru naraba will be with you

01:13.470 --> 01:20.210
Odayaka na hi o yume-mite

01:20.210 --> 01:27.440
Michi-naki tabiji wa tsuzuku

01:37.260 --> 01:38.690
Found it.

01:38.690 --> 01:40.350
Where?

01:44.470 --> 01:47.600
How tasteful of him.

01:47.600 --> 01:50.240
Oh, Ellis...

01:50.240 --> 01:52.370
Let's go together.

01:52.370 --> 01:55.810
To our place of eternity.

01:55.810 --> 01:58.580
Wiñay Marka.

01:58.580 --> 02:02.450
Caution is required when dealing with L.A.

02:17.830 --> 02:20.340
- Gracias.
- Ciao.

02:20.340 --> 02:22.800
Ellis, thanks for waiting.

02:24.770 --> 02:28.280
Oh, you still had that thing?

02:28.280 --> 02:29.540
Yup.

02:29.540 --> 02:31.650
Now, then...

02:31.650 --> 02:33.310
Ellis!

02:40.620 --> 02:43.460
Sorry, mister! My mistake!

02:43.460 --> 02:45.230
R-Right...

02:45.230 --> 02:46.750
Ellis?

02:55.300 --> 02:57.610
What's wrong?

02:57.610 --> 03:00.480
Oh, dear... It got crushed.

03:00.480 --> 03:02.270
Poor thing.

03:03.910 --> 03:06.780
Hey, what's with the attitude?

03:06.780 --> 03:08.650
That was an accident.

03:08.650 --> 03:12.520
I thought that guy was
after you, and that's why I...

03:12.520 --> 03:16.660
I knew that he didn't have a gun.

03:16.660 --> 03:19.590
What? Then say so first.

03:19.590 --> 03:22.720
You shoved me before I could tell you.

03:24.400 --> 03:26.870
Ellis, you know...

03:27.940 --> 03:30.210
Oh, wai... Hey!

03:30.210 --> 03:32.210
Hey, wait!

03:32.210 --> 03:33.870
Ellis!

03:36.640 --> 03:38.850
Oh, dear, I sense trouble.

03:38.850 --> 03:41.510
- Heading off in pursuit.
- Please do.

03:48.690 --> 03:53.360
Say, what do you want to do
about tonight's lodgings?

03:53.360 --> 03:54.700
Camping out...

03:54.700 --> 03:57.370
It gets cold at night around here.

03:57.370 --> 03:59.630
- There.
- Huh?

04:10.010 --> 04:11.950
It certainly looks like an inn.

04:11.950 --> 04:13.810
It is an inn.

04:21.620 --> 04:25.250
Huh... Kokopelli, is it?

04:37.470 --> 04:41.740
Oh, guests? Welcome.

04:44.050 --> 04:45.740
Hello.

04:49.750 --> 04:54.060
I see, so you're traveling,
just the two of you ladies, huh?

04:54.060 --> 04:56.360
It's complicated.

04:56.360 --> 05:00.830
But Grandpa, you sure have a lot of books.

05:00.830 --> 05:03.000
It's my work, you see.

05:03.000 --> 05:05.570
Well, I don't write anymore, though.

05:05.570 --> 05:08.340
"'Oh, Miguel...

05:08.340 --> 05:14.040
I've been in love with you since
the day I first laid eyes on you.'

05:14.040 --> 05:21.480
The incandescent flames of love
blazed in Miguel and Nadia's hearts."

05:21.480 --> 05:25.390
- That's...
- Ah, that brings back memories.

05:25.390 --> 05:28.490
Huh? Did you write that, Grandpa?

05:28.490 --> 05:30.390
Yes, when I was with my last...

05:30.390 --> 05:34.950
No, I wrote that when I was
with my second-to-last wife.

05:43.000 --> 05:46.440
Howard Heisman.

05:46.440 --> 05:48.380
I can't believe it.

05:48.380 --> 05:52.880
What's an author doing running
an inn way out in the country here?

05:52.880 --> 05:55.450
I retired 10 years ago, you see.

05:55.450 --> 05:57.020
You're alone?

05:57.020 --> 05:59.590
Yes, I'm alone now.

05:59.590 --> 06:02.690
- Care to be my wife, missy?
- No.

06:02.690 --> 06:05.120
What a plain-spoken missy you are.

06:06.790 --> 06:09.820
Oh? Could it be another guest?

06:11.670 --> 06:13.870
Ricardo!

06:13.870 --> 06:15.840
Hi, bonita.

06:15.840 --> 06:17.770
Acquaintances of yours?

06:17.770 --> 06:19.440
You could say that.

06:19.440 --> 06:21.780
We'd like lodgings for one night.

06:21.780 --> 06:23.810
Sure, you're welcome to stay here.

06:23.810 --> 06:26.980
Then, the missy and her
friend will be in Room 1.

06:26.980 --> 06:28.920
And you two will be in the next room over.

06:28.920 --> 06:31.420
- One more room.
- Huh?

06:31.420 --> 06:33.790
I'm separate from Nadie.

06:33.790 --> 06:35.780
Separate?

06:36.960 --> 06:40.430
Well, that's kind of how it is right now.

06:40.430 --> 06:41.930
I see.

06:41.930 --> 06:45.800
When you're on a long journey,
things like that are bound to happen.

06:45.800 --> 06:49.740
Then, missy, you take
the room at the very front.

06:49.740 --> 06:51.430
Got it.

07:02.120 --> 07:04.820
Some after-dinner herb tea.

07:04.820 --> 07:07.990
Thank you. That was delicious, Grandpa.

07:07.990 --> 07:09.890
You're a good cook.

07:09.890 --> 07:12.880
A ladies' man has to be a good cook.

07:18.070 --> 07:21.040
Oh, Kokopelli's flute, right?

07:21.040 --> 07:23.000
Right you are.

07:23.000 --> 07:26.510
- Kokopelli?
- He's the spirit of harvest.

07:26.510 --> 07:30.180
He's also known as the messenger
of peace, who brings happiness.

07:30.180 --> 07:33.820
You saw him at the entrance, remember?

07:33.820 --> 07:36.820
Oh, that drawing.

07:36.820 --> 07:38.980
You're very knowledgeable, Nadie.

07:44.160 --> 07:46.530
You suck.

07:46.530 --> 07:48.720
Here, let me see that for a sec.

07:50.930 --> 07:53.670
Wow, so it's not wood.

07:53.670 --> 07:55.070
It's llama bone.

07:55.070 --> 07:56.900
Llama...

07:56.900 --> 07:58.770
Do you know what llamas are?

08:00.240 --> 08:05.150
They have long necks like
this with ears that stand up.

08:05.150 --> 08:09.120
And their eyes are really far apart...

08:09.120 --> 08:11.140
- Nadie.
- Huh?

08:24.730 --> 08:28.070
Ellis? Ellis, I'm coming in.

08:28.070 --> 08:30.910
- No.
- Ellis.

08:30.910 --> 08:33.880
Because I suck at playing the flute.

08:33.880 --> 08:35.980
I wasn't really serious about that.

08:35.980 --> 08:37.740
I'm going to sleep now.

09:03.600 --> 09:06.610
Ellis, I'm here.

09:06.610 --> 09:08.170
Welcome.

09:10.010 --> 09:14.080
It's cold outside. Come on in.

09:14.080 --> 09:17.920
I didn't come here to see you.

09:17.920 --> 09:22.620
Such things are ill-suited to this place.

09:22.620 --> 09:24.820
Come on inside.

09:26.290 --> 09:28.830
Come.

09:28.830 --> 09:31.030
Good grief.

09:31.030 --> 09:33.190
What about you, young lady?

09:36.140 --> 09:38.640
I have some delicious herb tea.

09:38.640 --> 09:39.970
Who are you?

09:39.970 --> 09:42.740
Just an old man, as you can see.

09:44.650 --> 09:47.180
I find that hard to believe.

09:47.180 --> 09:51.650
Is that right? Then you leave me no choice.

09:51.650 --> 09:54.190
The truth is, I'm...

09:54.190 --> 09:55.950
...a spirit.

09:57.890 --> 10:01.200
Don't be ridiculous.

10:01.200 --> 10:04.030
When you feel like having
some tea, come on inside.

10:04.030 --> 10:05.900
You'll be made welcome.

10:10.610 --> 10:12.940
I'd like to request a background check.

11:03.390 --> 11:09.060
I heard the stories about Kokopelli
from my mom when I was little.

11:09.060 --> 11:15.340
I wanted to meet Kokopelli, so I
threw myself into practicing the flute.

11:15.340 --> 11:20.410
I felt like if I learned how to play,
he would come to see me.

11:20.410 --> 11:24.880
But I never did learn to play well.

11:24.880 --> 11:27.150
Children are innocent.

11:27.150 --> 11:29.880
They're easily hurt.

11:29.880 --> 11:34.890
Even things that adults
rationalize matter-of-factly,

11:34.890 --> 11:38.190
children are unable to rationalize.

11:38.190 --> 11:42.060
In terms of colors, children only
see things in black and white.

11:42.060 --> 11:46.090
- In other words...
- Love or hate.

11:53.840 --> 11:56.410
Who'd have thought that
you'd teach me something?

11:56.410 --> 11:58.150
Not very like me, eh?

11:58.150 --> 12:00.480
Is it thanks to Lirio?

12:00.480 --> 12:03.920
No, it was long before that...

12:03.920 --> 12:07.090
Something that happened so long
ago that I wish I could forget it,

12:07.090 --> 12:09.110
but it's stuck in my mind...

12:13.730 --> 12:15.500
I've talked too much.

12:15.500 --> 12:17.930
It seems I'm drunk tonight.

12:19.800 --> 12:22.340
- I'll decline.
- All right.

12:22.340 --> 12:24.130
Ricardo.

12:25.770 --> 12:27.740
Thank you.

12:27.740 --> 12:29.470
You're going to catch a cold.

12:54.100 --> 12:57.430
Ooh, it's seriously getting cold out here.

13:02.140 --> 13:03.940
Blue-eyes!

13:03.940 --> 13:05.980
That proprietor is an imposter.

13:05.980 --> 13:08.450
- What?
- I did a background check.

13:08.450 --> 13:12.150
Howard Heisman died three years ago.

13:27.430 --> 13:29.160
Ellis.

13:30.870 --> 13:32.010
What's that?

13:32.010 --> 13:35.240
- I looked into a mirror.
- A mirror?

13:35.240 --> 13:37.230
When I did...

13:39.580 --> 13:43.220
...I didn't have a nice look on my face.

13:43.220 --> 13:46.020
Are you hurting?

13:46.020 --> 13:47.420
Yes.

13:47.420 --> 13:49.560
I see.

13:49.560 --> 13:51.920
Come with me for a second.

13:53.860 --> 13:56.400
Then, who is that old man?

13:56.400 --> 14:01.170
Who knows? Just a plain con man, or maybe...

14:01.170 --> 14:03.170
A bounty hunter...

14:03.170 --> 14:05.140
That's a possibility.

14:05.140 --> 14:06.610
Ellis...

14:10.210 --> 14:12.310
My subordinates have gone in.

14:12.310 --> 14:15.510
Our superiors have told us to
take Ellis into safe custody.

14:16.980 --> 14:19.150
- It's beyond this door.
- Okay.

14:19.150 --> 14:22.060
Stop right there.

14:22.060 --> 14:25.130
What might be the meaning of this, young ladies?

14:25.130 --> 14:27.290
Hand over that girl.

14:43.540 --> 14:46.380
Move aside. I'm not letting you take Ellis.

14:46.380 --> 14:49.480
Ellis is missing a part of her memory.

14:49.480 --> 14:52.650
A part of her memory from
a very crucial time period.

14:52.650 --> 14:55.220
When you've arrived at your destination,

14:55.220 --> 14:57.920
do you think Ellis will find happiness?

15:00.460 --> 15:02.600
Hand over Ellis.

15:02.600 --> 15:06.630
Doing so will bring the
greatest happiness to her.

15:06.630 --> 15:08.970
The journey ends here.

15:08.970 --> 15:11.640
Let her go for her sake.

15:11.640 --> 15:14.480
Wiñay Marka is a place of eternity.

15:14.480 --> 15:18.010
Where is that place? What's there?

15:18.010 --> 15:20.980
You know, don't you? Tell me.

15:22.520 --> 15:24.590
Blue-eyes.

15:24.590 --> 15:27.250
Don't be deceived, Nadie.

15:29.520 --> 15:31.250
L. A...

15:34.230 --> 15:37.360
What that woman is saying is nonsense.

15:37.360 --> 15:43.270
Arriving at Wiñay Marka is precisely
what will bring happiness to my Ellis.

15:43.270 --> 15:45.410
What's there?

15:45.410 --> 15:47.540
Think about it, Nadie.

15:47.540 --> 15:53.350
If he wants to get there, there is
no happiness waiting for Ellis there.

15:53.350 --> 15:55.680
His sinister design is all that there is.

15:55.680 --> 15:58.050
Sinister design, is it?

15:58.050 --> 16:01.090
Am I wrong?

16:01.090 --> 16:04.160
It looks to me that you have
your own sinister design, too.

16:04.160 --> 16:06.660
All I'm doing is following orders.

16:06.660 --> 16:08.390
I wonder...

16:11.530 --> 16:15.000
So, what's there? Tell me.

16:15.000 --> 16:19.570
Once you know, you'll end up
agonizing even more...

16:19.570 --> 16:22.060
It's sure to bring you suffering.

16:23.280 --> 16:25.350
That much, we agree on.

16:25.350 --> 16:29.380
All you have to do is safely deliver Ellis.

16:29.380 --> 16:32.320
No, I won't let you go.

16:32.320 --> 16:34.050
Do you really mean it?

16:36.220 --> 16:38.050
I really mean it.

17:10.220 --> 17:12.090
Nadie!

17:12.090 --> 17:14.360
Ricardo... Hey, did you just...

17:14.360 --> 17:16.800
Ellis has disappeared!

17:16.800 --> 17:19.400
This is it. Try opening it, Ellis.

17:19.400 --> 17:20.800
Okay.

17:45.660 --> 17:47.420
It's beautiful.

17:52.130 --> 17:54.170
It's glowing.

17:54.170 --> 17:56.740
How do you feel, Ellis?

17:56.740 --> 17:58.840
Different than the other day...

17:58.840 --> 18:03.140
When it was glowing the
other day, my chest felt tight.

18:03.140 --> 18:06.110
It hurt a lot.

18:06.110 --> 18:09.410
But now, it doesn't hurt.

18:25.300 --> 18:27.160
Nadie...

18:41.120 --> 18:42.780
Nadie...

19:11.410 --> 19:15.220
Ellis?! Ellis!

19:15.220 --> 19:18.450
Ellis!

19:18.450 --> 19:19.890
Ellis...

19:19.890 --> 19:22.760
Nadie...

19:22.760 --> 19:24.220
Ellis...

19:24.220 --> 19:25.830
Ellis!

19:25.830 --> 19:28.620
- Nadie...
- Sorry...

19:31.630 --> 19:33.300
I'm sorry.

19:33.300 --> 19:36.500
No, I was the one in the wrong.

19:38.940 --> 19:42.510
I have no happy memories,

19:42.510 --> 19:45.780
so even the little things are important to me.

19:45.780 --> 19:49.180
They're really important to me.

19:49.180 --> 19:54.960
Yeah, you're right. I'll remember that.

19:54.960 --> 19:56.920
You know what, Nadie?

19:56.920 --> 19:59.860
- Hm?
- I'm glad.

19:59.860 --> 20:02.500
Ellis...

20:02.500 --> 20:06.530
You and I are friends, right?

20:06.530 --> 20:09.400
You dummy, of course we are.

20:09.400 --> 20:12.860
Let's go together, to Wiñay Marka.

20:14.680 --> 20:17.410
Yes, let's go.

20:17.410 --> 20:20.710
I don't know what awaits us there.

20:20.710 --> 20:25.590
But if Ellis wants to go, we'll go.

20:25.590 --> 20:29.860
No matter what's there,
I'll stay by Ellis's side...

20:29.860 --> 20:32.620
...and I'll protect her.

20:49.840 --> 20:51.880
Doug.

20:51.880 --> 20:54.550
Oh, Melissa.

20:54.550 --> 20:58.490
- Doug...
- Let's go shopping in town today.

20:58.490 --> 21:00.250
I'm so happy!

21:01.660 --> 21:03.920
It's a beautiful day.

21:06.290 --> 21:08.660
Okay, we're going on ahead.

21:08.660 --> 21:11.290
What? Ahead?

21:15.770 --> 21:18.040
Bye-bye, bonita.

21:18.040 --> 21:20.040
Did you find Grandpa?

21:20.040 --> 21:21.910
Didn't find him.

21:21.910 --> 21:24.410
I see.

21:24.410 --> 21:27.510
I wonder where he went so early in the morning.

21:27.510 --> 21:30.720
I wanted to say goodbye.

21:30.720 --> 21:34.020
He probably went home. Let's go.

21:34.020 --> 21:37.490
Went home? Well, whatever.

21:37.490 --> 21:40.360
We'll try dropping by again
on the way back or something.

21:40.360 --> 21:43.920
- Bye-bye.
- Bye-bye, Grandpa.

21:54.740 --> 21:57.810
Ellis?

21:57.810 --> 22:00.470
Ellis, where are you?

22:14.390 --> 22:16.390
What does this mean?

22:21.800 --> 22:24.570
I do not believe in ghosts.

22:24.570 --> 22:31.680
However, it is certain that there are
truths stranger than fiction out there...

22:31.680 --> 22:33.610
...apparently.

22:36.550 --> 22:40.350
Owaranai natsu no you ni

22:40.350 --> 22:43.790
Chiranai hana no you ni

22:43.790 --> 22:47.690
Dakishimeta sono ude o

22:47.690 --> 22:55.830
Zutto hanasanaide ite yo

23:02.040 --> 23:05.650
Sugari-tsuite-mitemo

23:05.650 --> 23:11.450
Mune wa mada chigau hakanasa de

23:11.450 --> 23:15.420
Toki no rizumu kazoeteru

23:15.420 --> 23:19.530
Akai hoshi no yoru

23:19.530 --> 23:23.530
Kiete-yuku nukumori

23:23.530 --> 23:27.470
Tsunagi-tometai no yo

23:27.470 --> 23:33.870
Hitomi tojita kimi o

23:33.870 --> 23:37.840
Akogare o kuri-kaeshi

23:37.840 --> 23:41.180
Doko e mo yukenaku-temo

23:41.180 --> 23:45.420
Setsunasa no tachidomaru

23:45.420 --> 23:51.730
Kono hito-toki ga futari no

23:51.730 --> 23:56.720
Subete yo
